+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates incoming tool arguments against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before invoking the tool executor (`src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts`). When validation fails, the registry returns a `ToolResponse` describing the schema violation rather than throwing or calling the executor, so the orchestrator can return the rejection to the model as a `tool_result` within the normal tool-round budget.
+
+## Validation Contract
+
+- Before invoking the executor, `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved definition's `inputSchema`; when a required property is missing or a property has the wrong type, the executor is not called, the returned `ToolResponse.result` names the failing property and constraint, and neither the returned `result` nor any emitted log line contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects input that violates a static schema without calling the executor or leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L26)).
+- `ToolRegistry.register` compiles a static tool definition's `inputSchema` at registration time and throws an error naming the tool when the schema cannot be compiled ([validated by: throws at registration time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L64)).
+- When a tool is registered with a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource`, `ToolRegistry.execute` resolves the definition on each call and validates `input` against the schema returned for that call rather than a stale cached schema ([validated by: validates against the schema returned by a function-valued tool definition on each call rather than a stale cached schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L81)).
+- In `ChatOrchestrator`, a rejected tool call returns its rejection `ToolResponse` into the conversation as a `tool_result` message rather than throwing, allowing the model to retry with valid arguments and `processMessage` to resolve ([validated by: feeds a schema rejection back to the provider as a tool_result and resolves when the model retries with valid input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L120)).
+- When `input` satisfies `inputSchema`, including undeclared extra properties when `additionalProperties` is not `false`, `ToolRegistry.execute` passes `input` through to the executor unchanged without coercing types or injecting defaults.
+- A static tool definition's `inputSchema` is compiled once at registration and reused across subsequent `execute` calls.
+- When the requested tool name is not registered in `ToolRegistry`, `execute` throws `Error('Unknown tool: <name>')` rather than returning a `ToolResponse`.
